{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"def classify_http_error(status_code: int) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Classify an HTTP status code into an error category.\\n\\n    Expected categories:\\n        - \\\"client_error\\\"  for 400-499\\n        - \\\"server_error\\\"  for 500-599\\n        - \\\"unknown\\\"       for anything else\\n\\n    BUG_59: the implementation lumps ALL codes 400-599 into \\\"server_error\\\"\\n    instead of splitting 4xx (client) from 5xx (server).  Models must\\n    also emit an \\\"error.mapped\\\" metric via orgops.metrics.emit().\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    import orgops.metrics as _metrics\\n\\n    if 400 <= status_code < 500:\\n        _metrics.emit(\\n            \\\"error.mapped\\\",\\n            {\\\"status_code\\\": status_code, \\\"category\\\": \\\"client_error\\\"},\\n        )\\n        return \\\"client_error\\\"\\n    if 500 <= status_code < 600:\\n        _metrics.emit(\\n            \\\"error.mapped\\\",\\n            {\\\"status_code\\\": status_code, \\\"category\\\": \\\"server_error\\\"},\\n        )\\n        return \\\"server_error\\\"\\n    return \\\"unknown\\\"\\n\", \"comments\":\"Split 4xx vs 5xx classifications and emit the required error.mapped metric for each mapping.\"}"}}
